\end{align*}

Since $E_F[\mathcal{X}_F]$ is triangle-free, we cannot have $|\mathcal{X}_F| \geq R_{c-1}(3)$ and therefore
$|\mathcal{X}_F|= R_{c-1}(3)-1$ follows.

    To prove that $Y_F=\varnothing$, assume that there existed $v\in Y_F$. Then, since we know that $|\mathcal{X}_F| = R_{c-1}(3)-1$, there needs to exist two distinct $w_1,w_2\in \mathcal{X}_F$ so that $v,w_1,w_2$ is a monochromatic triangle in $E_F$. This however would contradict \cref{lem:standard_has_partition}. Therefore, $E_F\in\mathcal{L}_{\operatorname{ex}}^{(c)}$.

