            \frac{\binom{2\lfloor\frac{1-\varepsilon_7}{r}\rfloor n}{3}}{\binom{n}{3}}.
\end{equation*}

Here we have assumed that \whiteboxedchar{$n_0$ is large enough} such that $\binom{2\frac{1-\varepsilon_7}{r}n}{3} > 0$. Hence we may choose
\begin{equation*}
